From: postmarketOS
Subject: samsung-sit: stop bearer connects from rewriting the attach APN

SET_INITIAL_ATTACH_APN names the APN the CP puts in its ATTACH REQUEST and the
CP keeps whatever it was last told, so it is modem-wide state rather than a
property of any one context. The connect sequence sent it anyway, with the APN
of the bearer being brought up: 'ims' for the IMS PDN and "" for a bearer that
names none.

Measured against this modem's own Android, on the same two SIMs. Android sends
SET_INITIAL_ATTACH_APN four times per boot -- twice per stack, and only ever
the carrier's attach entry, 'sp.telus.com' for Telus and 'mobile.bm' for Fizz;
across a 41342-record capture that includes calls it sends it six times, and
never with 'ims' or "". One of our boots sent it 21 times: 'sp.telus.com' x15,
'ims' x4, "" x2.

An attach APN the HSS does not know draws ESM cause 27 (missing or unknown
APN); the CP retries, gives up with EMM cause 10 (implicitly detached) and from
there refuses every PDN with MATCH_ALL_RULE_NOT_ALLOWED (2253), the IMS one
included, so there is no VoLTE. Neither indication appears anywhere in the
Android capture.

Drop the step. The attach APN now has exactly two owners: the power-up path,
which seeds it from the carrier's IA (or DEFAULT) entry before the radio goes
on, and SetInitialEpsBearerSettings. Both go through one resolver, so the
cause-10 recovery also falls back to the carrier entry instead of doing nothing
when no profile has been configured -- which is the case this is meant to fix,
since needing a configured profile was the gsm.initial-eps-bearer-apn
workaround.

--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-client.c
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-client.c
@@ -2513,10 +2513,32 @@
